# Project Responsive Rules

The current UI was designed for one desktop screen size.

Preserve the existing visual design language, but do not preserve fixed dimensions that prevent responsive behavior.

## Target Viewports

Always consider and test:

- 1920px — Large Desktop
- 1440px — Desktop
- 1280px — Small Desktop
- 1024px — Laptop
- 768px — Tablet
- 390px — Mobile
- 375px — Small Mobile

## Design Preservation

Preserve:

- Colors
- Visual style
- Component appearance
- Information hierarchy
- Business logic

Responsive implementation may change:

- Width
- Height
- Padding
- Gap
- Grid columns
- Component arrangement
- Sidebar behavior
- Table behavior
- Typography sizing when necessary

Do not redesign the UI unless required for smaller screens.

## Layout

Do not build layouts for only one fixed screen resolution.

Prefer:

- Flexible width
- CSS Grid
- Flexbox
- minmax()
- auto-fit / auto-fill
- clamp()
- max-width
- Container Queries when appropriate

Avoid unnecessary fixed widths and absolute positioning.

## Sidebar

Desktop:

- Keep full sidebar where sufficient space exists

Tablet / Mobile:

- Collapse sidebar
- Use hamburger navigation
- Open as drawer / overlay

## Tables

Desktop:

- Keep full table whenever possible

Smaller screens:

- Hide non-critical columns
- OR use table container horizontal scrolling
- OR convert to mobile card layout

Never allow the entire page to horizontally scroll.

## Forms

Desktop:

- Multi-column allowed

Tablet:

- Reduce columns when needed

Mobile:

- Prefer single column

## Responsive Audit

Before considering a page complete, check:

1920
1440
1280
1024
768
390
375

Check for:

- Horizontal overflow
- Sidebar issues
- Header overlap
- Table overflow
- Modal overflow
- Broken grids
- Text clipping
- Button overlap
- Incorrect spacing
